    "body": "I had to change from taking a borrow of the context variable to taking a clone. Here's why: when using the logical path, we read `$PWD` from the environment to construct a PathBuf. Since the PathBuf is created within the scope of the match, it's dropped at the closing brace, so there's no way to return a borrow of it without having the reference outlive the data.\r\n\r\nThere are two alternate solutions to this:\r\n  - Set up `use_logical_path` as a prompt-wide config which controls how the `context` determines the `current_dir`\r\n  - Declare a mutable outside the match block, set its value within the match, then return a reference to it.",
