    "body": "As far as falling back to physical path goes: that's actually the intention of this code, so I guess I need to add some comments to make that clear. If the logical path is unreadable, we log an error and ~return None~ assign `None` to the logical path value (this is just so that the user will have a clue as to why the behavior has changed).\r\n\r\nFurther down, `None` values are converted into the physical path (or at least, the path returned by `std::env::current_dir`, which might not actually be the physical path).\r\n\r\nThe total effect of this is that if `use_logical_path` is false OR `PWD` is unreadable, the prompt will fall back to the physical path.",
    "created_at": "2019-09-16T23:31:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-20T16:00:31Z",
